> netwk, can it store DOS/WIN format files?  Can it run UNIX or is the
> Open VMS a good OS to use in such an environment?

I answered that on your previous post in another newsgroup.

You have a system that has 2 VUPS, and a minimal amount of disk space.

larger DSSI disks are still in good supply, but may cost more than replacing
your system with a faster used VAXstation.

Also faster q-bus CPUs and Memory have been seen available cheap, but they
require you to get an eithernet controller, and they seem to still be worth
something.

If you decide to get rid of it, post on comp.os.vms and comp.sys.dec and
someone will be interested.

> WOULD LOVE A LONG DETAILED DISCUSSION FROM YA'LL.

There are several Q-bus VAX hackers hanging arround on comp.os.vms.  Please
look up my previous response to you.

See: http://www.montagar.com/hobbyist, and follow the links.

Also see the OpenVMS FAQ available at http://www.openvms.digital.com/

