Hoff

FYI

I heard, from several USERS to whom we sell, have been given VMS or Unix
licenses for their PWS 433a 500a 600a systems (NOT -AU)

IF, ... IF Compaq doesn't offically support VMS and UNIX on the PWS, then
why are they giving them licenses to run these OS's on these systems ?

FYI - there is an internal listing within Compaq - that is supposedly only
for Compaq personnel, that tells how to convert a system from PWSxxxA to
an -AU

This "Conversion kit consists of:

1) KZPBA-CA (a Bog standard Q-Logic QLA1040)
2) An RRD46-AB (Bog std Toshiba 12x SCSI)
3) PBXGB-AA or now a PDXGK-BB (a bog standard ELSA Synergy PCI 8mb non-vivo)

There ya go - a VMS machine that runs at pretty much the same speed as an
Alphastation 500/500

Hmmmm.... And the -A was SO much cheaper than the AU

If I remember right, the guy that told me this stuff at DECpaq, was saying
it was a field service option only, but would cost around $3000

Still a bit cheaper than buying the original -AU ?!

Regards to all

David Turner



