:Then (again) I think it was yesterday that I dialed that number and
:eventually ended up speaking to someone in the OpenVMS support group.
:According to what he told me OpenVMS runs on the Alpha Personal Workstation
:433a (as well as Tru64). I forget about the issue of someone in the OpenVMS
:support group giving definitive answers with regard to Tru64 . . .
:
:Last night I happened to be looking for info on the web site (never an easy
:task) and found numerous pieces of information (some of which had that
:"Hoff" look and feel) to the effect that - OpenVMS doesn't run on the 433a
:as these are (were) designed with NT (ha ha) - and Windoz (if I remember
:correctly) in mind.

  Microsoft Windows NT (and its follow-on Microsoft Windows (for numeric
  suffixes for values 2000 and more) was the target for the PWS-a box, and 
  it could also operate on the PWS-au box.  Microsoft Windows (for numeric 
  suffixes with values of 1999 and less) does not and can not operate on 
  Alpha...  Support for continued development of support for Microsoft 
  Windows NT is ending on Alpha, and support for its follow-on Microsoft 
  Windows (for numeric suffixes for values 2000 and more) was never 
  released as a product...  Got all that? :-)

  There were various upgrades from PWS-a to PWS-au, but there is presently
  no support for OpenVMS on the PWS-a series per the SPD and the OpenVMS
  Product Managers -- I was discussing this with the relevent OpenVMS 
  product managers just yesterday.  There are various cases where you can 
  apparently (clearly) get this to work, and there are cases where it 
  does not work, and there are then the discussions of the support of the
  various I/O widgets...

  As the systems are not listed in the OpenVMS SPD, they are not considered 
  to be officially supported.

  I have been working with the product managers to get support extended, 
  or to get the systems converted (somehow) to -au series boxes (various
  of which are supported), or get some other official statement of (non)
  support in this area.


