The 64bit Linux market has been dominated by Alpha since its
inception.  If the Merced is expensive, it won't have much effect on
that market, and neither would a similar-priced Alpha; most people
would continue to buy cheaper Alphas.  I give Sledgehammer a much
better chance on taking over the 64-bit Linux market than IA-64 (and
only because Sledgehammer implementations will be credible IA-32
processors that happen to be 64-bit processors, too); or maybe this
market will just stay with Alphas.

