phaedrus@ultra.net.au wrote:
> 
> Can anyone tell me if the ST 506/SCSI and the SCSI/SCSI cards are
> interchangeable? I tried to use a ST506?SCSI in place of the shorter
> SCSI/SCSI card but it wont recognise the HDs' when I do a sh dev at
> the >>> prompt.
> Thankx, Darryl,Australia.

If by "interchangable", if you mean can you use either one in a VS3100,
then the answer is yes.

However, you do need to realize that they work differently.  In
particular, the SCSI/SCSI card has 2 SCSI busses (duh!).  One is
internal and one is external.  The SCSI/ST506 card combines the internal
and external busses into a single bus.

With a SCSI/SCSI card, you can have internal and external devices that
are set to the same SCSI ID.  If you replace the SCSI/SCSI card with a
SCSI/ST506 card, these devices will conflict with each other.

Also, with the SCSI/ST506 card, the internal cable must be in place even
if you don't have any internal devices.  If it is not in place, the
external bus will not be connected.  The chain runs from the controller
card, through the interal bus, back into the controller card and out the
external connector.

The SCSI/SCSI card's external bus will still work if the internal cable
is missing (since they are separate busses).

Good luck!

