  I have 2 - one about 4 months old and one that just came (new from Compaq)
last week.

  I just looked, and the VMS version with 128MB was discontinued earlier this
month (DY-55NJA-CA) but it's available in a refurbished model (DY-55NJA-CV).
The 256MB, 512MB, and 1GB versions are all still available, with a 10 day
lead time. They're also available refurbished with a 30 day lead time and a
substantial savings ($27,485 for a new 1GB box, $19,000 for a refurb).

  The Tru64 and Linux 128MB versions were also discontinued.

  I would expect Compaq to announce a faster processor in the future and not
discontinue this box. Further, the DS20E (which is a different form factor
and *not* a replacement product) was never offered with 128MB. I think that
discontinuing the 128MB models was just a belated realization that 128MB just
isn't enough memory these days.

  I'm not sure what options you couldn't get for this box - aside from the
situation with the graphics cards (Elsa at the low end and 300/350 at the
high end and nothing in the middle) almost all PCI options should be sup-
ported on this box. Most of the older ones (like the H8520-AA) haven't had
their descriptions updated, but they do work in the DS20.

  The Alpha Configuration Utility:
