    Thank you for your reply.  What kind of SCSI Drive controllers are in
your box?  Do you, or more importantly, will you have any desire to upgrade
them?  If you are like me in this regard you will be disappointed to
discover that this kind of technical upgrade, simple as it sounds as a "PCI
option", will not be available for the DS-20.  The Ultra-II-SCSI are
STANDARD on the DS-20E, but , I have been informed by Compaq that these
cards will not be available for the DS-20.  Given the functional
similarities between the DS20 andthe DS20E and the apparent focus of
upgradability on the DS20E, it appears the latter model is certainly the
"favored son" even if not a true replacement!

Mark




