Mark Weiner <mweiner@mail.med.upenn.edu> writes:
>     Thank you for your reply.  What kind of SCSI Drive controllers are in
> your box?  Do you, or more importantly, will you have any desire to upgrade
> them?

  Just about everything. There's the motherboard SCSI which Compaq doesn't
seem to admit to (there are 2 68-pin connectors on the motherboard, but I
don't think they actually do anything). I have a KZPCM-DA which is a re-
badged IntraServer product (ITI-4280UE), a KZPAC-CB 3-port RAID controller
(re-badged Mylex DAC960), a KZPBA-CA (re-badged Q-logic ISP-10x0) and a
KZPBA-CB (likewise, but differential SCSI).

  The only SCSI controller from the set available for the DS20E that isn't
specifically listed for the DS20 is the SN-KZPCA-AA "Single channel LVD
adapter". It's possible that they just didn't qualify the option on prior
systems. www.digital.com is unreachable right now or I'd look it up.

> If you are like me in this regard you will be disappointed to
> discover that this kind of technical upgrade, simple as it sounds as a "PCI
> option", will not be available for the DS-20.  The Ultra-II-SCSI are
> STANDARD on the DS-20E, but , I have been informed by Compaq that these
> cards will not be available for the DS-20.

  Who said this? Many people claim to speak for Compaq, and a lot of them
are uninformed/misinformed. I could fish out the DS20 product manager's
business card (I think I still have it) and mail them and ask. That would
be an authoritative answer.

> Given the functional
> similarities between the DS20 andthe DS20E and the apparent focus of
> upgradability on the DS20E, it appears the latter model is certainly the
> "favored son" even if not a true replacement!

  You could always add an IntraServer 6000-series Ultra 2 card. See
http://www.intraserver.com/download/docs/6000.pdf. This will get you your
choice of one or two Ultra2 buses, optionally with a bus translator to
support legacy single-ended devices without slowing down the SCSI bus.

  IntraServer are the folks who make the KZPCM-DA card for Compaq. They
also make the SCSI and Fast Ethernet adapters for some older VAXes which
Compaq also sells.

