I too have an 8530, with it's Pro380 console including the console hardware
module in it.
(You need that too) with the console software installed on the Pro.  I lack
only the special
cable from the console to the Vax, or I would have had it up and running by
now.
I also have the original console software on 5&1/4" Floppy, so I may be able
to help you with that.
I had to re-install it on the Pro myself, as the Pro's Hard disk had died
and it took some
scrounging to find (and format) a suitable replacement.

If you can't get a Pro380 WITH the Vax Console card, AND the Software
AND the Cable, you are dead in the water.  There is no other way to make it
work, AFAIK.

It also needs an RS232 cable from the pro to the vax for the terminal part
of the console
system, but that's less of a problem.  The big parallel cable is essential,
and I haven't been
able to track one down.  I'd be asking the lab it came from what happened to
console and cable.
They MUST have had them to make the beast work.

Now if you had a Vax 6000, it's a piece of cake, so if they throw one of
them out, grab it!

I hope your air conditioning is in good working order, 8530's throw out some
heat.

