There should be a fail-safe boot jumper on the motherboard (don't have
manuals near me, but look in the hardware manual (seen it on Digital's
website)).  You set this jumper and it boots off the floppy drive
before anything else (basically designed to be able to recover from a
bad firmware upgrade (or your problem)).  btw, you seem to have SRM
installed at the moment, not ARC.

The jumper isn't that hard to find once you know which one it is. :)

