|> Will tcpdump on DEC UNIX allow monitoring of the loopback interface?

Yes, at least on Digital UNIX V4.0F (perhaps not on some earlier releases):

% tcpdump -i lo0 icmp
Packet filter data-link type 7 unknown
Assuming Ethernet
tcpdump: listening on lo0
Using kernel BPF filter
17:39:03.866246 localhost > localhost: icmp: echo request
17:39:03.866322 localhost > localhost: icmp: echo reply
17:39:04.865656 localhost > localhost: icmp: echo request
17:39:04.865725 localhost > localhost: icmp: echo reply
