> however, the problem mostly goes away (you don't see it very often,
> except once in a while in some programs).  However, as a side-effect,
> ^Q's pop up in programs like Emacs (and other stuff), and it gets
> annoying.  Does anyone know what combination of terminal settings /
> linux settings I should use to make this think function optimally
> without quirkiness?

In my slackware 7.0 system, under /usr/doc/Linux-HOWTOs/, there's a
Text-Terminal-HOWTO.  In this howto is information regarding the VT's
hardware flow control.  I'll sum up informatin here for you.

The VTs use DTR/DSR flow control.  Linux uses RTS/CTS flow control.  Since
these are on physically different wires, these two wont work.. without
re-wiring.  The HOWTO specifically lists which wires to interconnect.  In
essence, you simply hook DTR to cts and DSR to rts (or something like that..
I dont have it out right now).  Anyway, this should fix your flow control
woes and let you use your 420 at a full 38.4k =)

-Jonas




