  Everything in the CMOS is maintained by the battery on this motherboard.
If you pop the battery out and wait a while for the charge to dissipate,
then re-install the battery, you'll clear the CMOS settings. Obviously, you
do all of this with the power off.

  NOTE: Someone posted here that after they did this their system no longer
worked at all. In all the cases I'm personally familiar with, this has never
happened. But do it at your own risk and don't blame me, etc.

