First of all you would need ClearVision management tool to setup that
DEChub 900. Though the initial/basic setup should work just fine.

The DECserver 900TM modules should attach to "thinwire" segment on
the DEChub 900 backplane. Same should happen also with all 90 modules.

So, use one of those DECrepeater 90T-16 ports to connect the DEChub 900
to the rest of the network. Using the DEChub 900 management port you can
assing ip address to a module on DEChub 900. I am not sure if the
DECrepeater
90 can provide IP management stack for the DEChub 900. You can always
try.

Now the DECserver 900 boots either from FLASH ram module (should be
clearly visible if you have them, kind of PC card) or using MOP or 
BOOTP/TFTP via network.

So, if you do not have DECserver 900 software on a flashram module, you
will
need to install approriarite software on your host and do the tricks so
in can "donate" WWENG2.SYS to the DECserver via network.

Remember that those DECserver 900 have serial port 1 as a sort of
console.
Hook up a terminal with 9600, 1 stop bit, No Parity, Eight bit data to 
serial line #1 and observer that the DECserver 900 reports.

I hope you have enough power modules on your DEChub 900. If the hub
does not have enough power to support all modules, priority is that
all 90 modules get power first, then we start with 900 modules starting
from DEChub 900 slot #1 towards slot #8.

The LED display on the hub should indicate how much power you have etc.

_veli

