Hi John,

There is nothing special with the ports on the 90T-16.
Just the same as on any other Multiport Repeater, the only
difference is the LAN connection on the backplane connector.
There are several LAN busses on the Multiswitch 900 backplane,
how much and which one depends largely on the installed firmware.
But if you have only *90* modules(no 900�s) you can only use one
LAN since those modules are smaller and connect only to one connector
in the backplane.
Also note, if you plug the modules into the backplane you cannot use
the thinwire connector(termination issues)!
The 900TM�s in contrast fit into both connectors and you have to configure
them onto one of six LANs. You do this via software called ClearVision
Multichassis Manager http://www.cabletron.com/digital/dr/npg/mqdaa-mn.html
Check out if the modules are configured to the same LAN "channel", otherwise
there would be NO connection between the modules.

For more information and some docs you should look at:
http://www.cabletron.com/digital/dr/npg/index-fm.html

cheers
Robert Schmoelzer
Telemed Communications, Austria

