Well, maybe I'll have to take a closer look at FreeBSD on the Alpha, then.
I had no idea there was any support for the 3000s at all.

In NetBSD/VAX land, "net-bootable only" is pretty much a codeword for "the
SCSI interface isn't supported". The OS doesn't know how to run disks on
the platform. You can boot the thing over the net and run it as a diskless
workstation. You'll need a MOP server for the machine supplying the system
image. The NetBSD VAX pages have some information on setting up a diskless
system. See http://vaxine.bitcon.no/section3.html#ss321
