You may want to check out NetBSD for the VAX.  VMS is also available (with a
hobbyist license).  That should cover you in the OS realm.  NetBSD
can be installed over the network (without needing any tapes) from another
unix box.

As far as your hardware goes, MicroVAX have hideous consoles, so you'll 
probably not get much information from that.  You may want to take a look
at the cards that are installed and search for what they are on the net.
The netBSD home page (www.netbsd.org) has some good VAX info pointers
on it.

You may also hunt up the VMS FAQ which does have some information on the
MicroVAX II hardware (the switches on the back, etc).  

Its not a fast machine, but there's something really cool about old
DEC hardware.

