Scott Risdal wrote:

> ...we are attaching it externally using the cabinet for an HP SCSI
> DAT drive.  We configured the dip switches on the Seagate
> drive(ST34520N) to SCSI ID 2 and removed the terminator jumper since we
> will be putting it first in line with our existing external CD-ROM.  The
> odd thing is that the HP enclosure also has a little clicker on the back
> to allow setting the SCSI address, I set this to 2 as well.  Seems like
> the the thing to do.

I don't know who opened the HP enclosure, but if I'm right, the little
numberswitch is connected with a small bundle of colored wires to the
id-select jumper block on the tape drive. If that is the case, and it is
not reconnected to the disk drive, the numberswitch is not relevant.

I guess you have done the smart thing to check if ID 2 is not used in
any other device. Also check if the internal and external SCSI chains
are not two ends of the same chain.

Also, there is the possibility of half-termination when you attach a
(small) SCSI device with a converter cable to a wide SCSI bus, and
terminate that.

-- 
Alex

