In article <bGTn4.413$QN6.6180@news.optonline.net>, "Frank Sapienza" <sapienza@noesys.com> writes:
:>   Hmmm. Are you sure it's Q-bus? Given that the Q-bus does about 
:>   3 MB/sec on a good day, Fast SCSI is 10MB/sec and Ultra SCSI is 
:>   20MB/sec (in narrow mode, in wide mode they're twice that), I 
:>   don't see what this does for people.
:Yep, there's one for Q-bus.  The part number is DS-KZCCA-CB.
..

  The KZCCA connects to the CDAL (the CVAX chip bus), not the Q-bus...
  (This is the same bus that the integrated DSSI connectors typically
  connect into...)

  Other common options include the KZQSA (CD-ROM and tapes only), the
  KFQSA/HSD or other DSSI/HSD, and third-party Q-bus to SCSI widgets...

 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
   Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com




