David M. Razler <david.razler@worldnet.att.net> writes:
> The PDPs-14 and 16 were more custom controllers than computers per se.

The PDP-14 is a computer by most recent and sensible definitions of the work.
It has an instruction set and executes stored programs.

A "custom controller" may or may not be (or include) a computer.  A PDP-14
may be used as part of a "custom controller", but that doesn't make it any
less of a computer.

The PDP-16 is a computer construction set.  The PDP-16 is intended to be
configured as a computer, but can be configured in such a way as to not
be a computer.  The PDP-16 doesn't have a predefined instruction set.



