Hi,

I work for a company that has a DEC Alpha Workstation 600a with 512 meg
RAM, running Windows NT 4.0, SP 5.

We use this machine exclusively for Finite Element Analysis (mathematical
structural simulation), and use two different FEA software packages,
ANSYS, and ProMechanica. These software packages have two things in
common: one, they both use a remote licensing scheme, and two, both
packages can end up using 100 percent of CPU cycles for long periods of
time (hours on end). I'm a little hazy on the license scheme, but
basically the local machine (the DEC) and a remote license server need to
periodically be able to contact each other to verify permission to run
