The PostScript cartridge may not be configured in the machine.

1. If the cartridge is properly configured in the printer, it will be in the
left most slot and when powered on, the printer will output a PostScript
test page.

2. If the cartridge is not properly configured in the printer, then the
printer will work as PCL device, and it will not print a PostScript test
page on power up.

3. To cause the printer to configure the cartridge, you need to power up the
printer with the cartridge in the left most slot, then, press and hold the
online button for 5 to 10 seconds. The unit will configure and then print a
PostScript test page.

rtt

