I've never had a Venturis FX motherboard in my hands to experiment
with.  The board does have a socket for an Intel-standard voltage
regulator module, so there is some possibility that it could run
either an Intel Pentium MMX CPU or an AMD K6 CPU.  But without trying
it, I can't recommend it.  For sure, you can upgrade to a Pentium 200,
but that won't boost performance more than 20%.  And Pentium 200 CPUs
continue to sell at a premium.

I'm almost dead certain you could install a 233MHz Pentium MMX using a
PowerLeap adapter.  The PowerLeap products are well-designed, and I've
never had a problem using them.

What size is the external cache memory?  The cache socket is also a
standard COAST (Cache On A STick) socket, so an upgrade to 512K would
make some sense, and may well boost performance by the same 20%.

Is the hard drive light flashing a lot?  If so, a memory upgrade would
cut down on swap file activity.  So would a 7200 rpm disk drive, as
you stated.  But more memory may well be more effective than a new
drive... Ben Myers

