We are looking for the following rare cards. They were usually connected
Encore/SEL/Gould computers to PDPs on the UNIBUS. They could be used in old
VAXes too. Some simulation sites may have had them. We are interested in the
PDP card - not the Encore side. The PDP cards were produced by

Software Applications Intl. Corp.
Computer System Products

in the early 1980s to early 1990s.

There were two varieties:

In the first there was a two card set. The SAI card was a model 3037 and it
was referred to as a SAI Compatiblity card which was connected to an Encore
HSD (High Speed Data) card by two 50 pin connectors for task to task
communication. The other card was a third party card that did the DMA; it
was an 'MDB' board.

