rnewman@thecia.net (Ron Newman) writes:
> No PDP-2 or PDP-3?  (Were there any such machines?)

None ever sold by DEC.  Reportedly the did have a paper design
for the PDP-3, and a DEC customer built one.

> No PDP-20?

There's no such critter.  You're probably thinking of the PDP-10, which
was used in both the DECsystem-10 and the DECSYSTEM-20.  There were four
major implementations of the PDP-10 processor, called the KA10, KI10, KL10,
and KS10.  The KL10 came in numerous variants, some of which are
occasionally referred to as KL20.  There was also a mostly-compatible
predecessor, the PDP-6 using a type 166 processor.

They only got as far as PDP-16, and they skipped 13.  I guess they must
have thought that 13 was unlucky.  Geez, I thought that in this
enlightened age everyone knew that it's bad luck to be superstitious.



