If you use the DEC 2200 Driver for Windows, the Windows machine will not
produce postscript, but native DEC PPL 3 mode. You should use the
drivers for a 2250 instead.

To switch your printer to postscript mode: (I hope the exact sequence is
correct)
- go OFFLINE (by pressing On Line switch).
- press Menu (it shows SETUP: INTERFACE)
- press > (shows: CONTROLLER MODE)
- press Enter (shows: MODE: PPL3)
- press > (shows: MODE: POSTSCRIPT)
- press Enter (shows: SELECTED)
- press OnLine to leave menu's and go online.

Now it should be in PostScript mode.

-- 
Karel van Houten
